<Layout title="About Cyber Reliant"><PageHero eyebrow="ABOUT CYBER RELIANT" title="A different starting point. The file itself." text="Cyber Reliant protects the path from stored fragments to readable information. Compromising storage alone does not reproduce that path." number="05"/>
<section class="section container about-statement"><div class="statement-mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 180 200"><path d="m15 55 75-40 75 40-75 40zM15 95l75 40 75-40v35l-75 40-75-40z" fill="currentColor"/></svg><span>CYBER RELIANT</span></div><div><span class="eyebrow">THE IDEA AT THE CENTER</span><h2>Infrastructure can change.<br/>The importance of your<br/>information doesn’t.</h2><p class="large-copy">Possessing the fragments is not the same as possessing the file.</p><p>Cyber Reliant separates protected file fragments from cryptographic material and controls how they come together. The authorized reconstruction path identifies the correct fragments, obtains required material, decrypts the pieces and rebuilds the file.</p><a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works">Understand the approach <Arrow/></a></div></section>
<section class="soft-section"><div class="section container"><span class="eyebrow">PRINCIPLES BEHIND THE APPROACH</span><h2>Designed around what matters.</h2><div class="use-case-grid"><article><span class="card-number">01</span><h3>Start with the data.</h3><p>Consider the sensitive file as a protection boundary, alongside infrastructure and identity controls.</p></article><article><span class="card-number">02</span><h3>Separate the paths.</h3><p>Protect file fragments and cryptographic material through distinct paths that meet at authorized reconstruction.</p></article><article><span class="card-number">03</span><h3>Make room for scrutiny.</h3><p>Evaluate implementation details, operational tradeoffs and evidence for the intended environment.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section container split-content"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE NEXT CHAPTER</span><h2>Extending the<br/>architecture.</h2></div><div><span class="outline-tag dark-tag">UPCOMING NETWORK VERSION</span><p class="large-copy">The file is fragmented. The cryptographic material is, too.</p><p>The upcoming network architecture fragments or shreds cryptographic material and protects multiple components through the HSM architecture. The separate file and key paths converge through authorized Cyber Reliant reconstruction.</p><a class="text-link" href="/technology#network">Explore what’s next <Arrow/></a></div></section><CTA title="Let’s start a substantive conversation."/></Layout>
